<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?><kml xmlns="http://www.opengis.net/kml/2.2"><Document><name>ILLUSTRATIVE amazon-leo-lv01 ascent</name><description>ILLUSTRATIVE ASCENT ECEF — Vulcan VC6L Amazon Leo LV-01 (SLC-41) — NOT OFFICIAL TELEMETRY
PRE-FLIGHT ILLUSTRATIVE. ULA Vulcan VC6L (first 6-SRB / first LEO-optimized Centaur V), 40 Amazon Leo satellites, SLC-41.
T0 2026-11-13T17:54:00Z (Fri Nov 13 9:54 a.m. PST / 12:54 p.m. EST) per ULA Vulcan Leo 1 page https://www.ulalaunch.com/missions/next-launch/vulcan-leo-1. LL2 Go, window 17:54–18:24Z (id ef9850ad-1096-425b-9d27-f7bbd186e61a). FAA ULA KV-01 primary 1754Z–1900Z, backup 11/14 1732Z–1838Z.
Event times: Northrop Grumman Propulsion Products Catalog p.39 GEM 63XL burn 87.3 s; ULA UG §2.1 SRB jettison ~100 s after burnout; ULA UG Fig. 2.1.1-2 TYPICAL CCSFS two-burn sequence (Approximate Times &amp; Values): BECO 292 s, stage sep 298 s, MES1 308 s, fairing 316 s — TYPICAL, not LV-01&#x27;s unpublished timeline.
MES1 cutoff T+908 s is an ASSUMED 600 s first burn (308+600), the same assumption as the 3DOF timeline, tuned to a 180 × 450 km transfer. MES2 at first apoapsis and +2 revs are in the sim file only. File ends at MES1 cutoff.
Azimuth 43.69 deg: great-circle bearing from the LL2 pad (28.583410N, 80.583036W) to the far-edge midpoint (36.3583N, 70.9750W) of NAVAREA IV 1078/26 Area A (launch corridor). Non-rotating i ~52.66 deg. Hazard-area azimuth kept (NOTAM-first); not retuned to the FCC 51.9 deg shell. https://space-notices.com/notice/nav-warning-NAVAREA%20IV%201078%2F26
Orbit: 450 km circular insertion is ASSUMED from Amazon KA-01 (Atlas V, same pad, 28 Apr 2025): &#x27;completed releasing all 27 satellites ... at an altitude of 280 miles (450 kilometers)&#x27; https://www.aboutamazon.com/news/innovation-at-amazon/project-kuiper-photos-internet-satellite-first-launch. LV-01 insertion is not on the ULA/Amazon LV-01 pages. This surrogate ends at MES1 on the ASSUMED 180 × 450 km transfer (180 km perigee is a labelled stand-in); 450 km circularization is MES2 in the sim.
Altitude knots (t s: km; times published typical sequence or ASSUMED MES1 cutoff, ALTITUDES ASSUMED = this board&#x27;s 3DOF sim at those times): 0:0, 87.3:32.9, 100:44, 292:212.9, 298:218.7, 308:227.9, 316:234.9, 908:180.2
Horizontal ground speed ASSUMED linear 0 -&gt; 7.514 km/s (circular v at 180.2 km geodetic MES1 altitude minus Earth rotation along Az) at T+908 s. File ends at MES1 cutoff.
Pad (LL2): 28.583410N -80.583036E. Frame: WGS-84 ECEF, positions km, velocities km/s.
Constant-azimuth rhumb Az=43.69 deg from pad. Velocity ECEF: v_horiz along Az + hdot Up in local ENU.
T0 used: 2026-11-13T17:54:00Z. Re-run with another T0 by shifting utc_iso only; ECEF geometry is Earth-fixed.</description>
